BIOS 
----

* Architecture : 16 bit, limited memory

* Boot Method : MBR - based (2 TB disk limit)

* Interface : Text based, keyboard navigation

* Bootloader : MBR bootloader

* Security : No secure boot

* Boot speed : Slower, sequential intialization

* Partition Support : MBR (4 primary partition)

* Extensiblity : Limited

* Compatability : Legacy systems


UEFI
----


* Architecture : 32 or 64 bit, supports larger memory

* Boot Method : GPT based (>2 TB disk limit)

* Interface : GUI based, Supports keyboard and mouse

* Bootloader : Loads OS directly from ESP

* Security : Supports secure boot

* Boot speed : Faster, parallel intialization

* Partition Support : GPT (128 primary partition)

* Extensiblity : Modular and extensible

* Compatability : Modern systems with BIOS compatablity



